      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do we need a capacity when the buffer is sized? IIUC the proposal requires that if a function parameter is a sized buffer then the argument must be a sized buffer whose size is at least as large.\n\nEDIT: AFAICT from the transform code, looks like these overloads are mainly just for consistency / to avoid a special case in the transform? If so that\u0027s fine.",
      "revId": "3633b0b6eaf27895b3d9984f6bb6153f1f4dcbb6",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
